---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Cookbook · Pace"
  description="Concrete recipes for every team: install, authorize, paste the routine prompt, verify. One marquee workflow per team (sales pipeline brief, engineering self-review, finance month-end, and more). Copy and ship."
  activeNav="cookbook"
  canonicalPath="/cookbook"
>
  <article class="usecases-page">
    <header class="usecases-header">
      <span class="usecases-eyebrow">Cookbook</span>
      <h1>The Pace cookbook</h1>
      <p class="usecases-lede">
        Recipes, not theory. Each card combines Pace skills with Claude Code's broader features (<a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/routines">Routines</a>, <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks">hooks</a>, <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents">sub-agents</a>, plan mode, <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp">MCP connectors</a>) and walks you through setup: install the plugins, authorize the connectors, paste the prompt, verify. One marquee recipe per team, plus shorter overview cards for adjacent workflows.
      </p>
    </header>

    <aside class="usecases-eng-callout">
      <div class="usecases-eng-callout-text">
        <span class="usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow">Engineering</span>
        <h2>The engineering cookbook lives on its own page.</h2>
        <p>Eighteen engineering skills, grouped into five workflows: the stacked-PR loop, plan + pressure-test, TDD + coverage, diagnose + secure, and prototype + ship. Each with trigger phrases, examples, and what to expect.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="usecases-eng-callout-cta" href="/cookbook/engineering">Open the engineering cookbook &nearr;</a>
    </aside>

    <nav class="usecases-toc" aria-label="Jump to a team">
      <span class="usecases-toc-label">Jump to a team</span>
